From 3047da12e81d63c51ae996014f332fe4fc83f5ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Serhii Nikolaichuk <nikolaichuk.s.f@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:28:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] attest: a media type for each message, no rrp_id or
 endorsements, and the requests' syntax checked

The attest-* wire as proposed for draft-novak-lamps-tacra-est in October 2026, with its CDDL.

Media types, one for each message type, as each EST message type has its own (RFC 7030, Section 3.2.4), with the
names the reference implementation uses. attest-initiate answers application/est-attest-initiate+json; attest-enroll
takes application/est-attest-enroll+json; attest-retrieve takes application/est-attest-retrieve+json and answers
application/est-attest-bundle+json. The routes with a CA label take the same as those without (RFC 7030, Section
3.2.2); they took only application/json, which no attest-* resource takes now. Any other type is refused with 415 and
an Accept header that names the resource's type (RFC 9110, Section 15.5.16): the type and subtype compared without
regard to case, its parameters not considered, and a type that only begins with the resource's refused. The client
sends these types and checks the responses' types.

The attest-initiate response. It no longer carries rrp_id: the Attester binds the identifier of the Relying Party it
holds for the Target and mode, never one from the CAS (TACRA, "Binding Credential Keys to Evidence"). Nor
required_bindings, which no draft defines, nor server_id, which the backend never set. The server still checks the
RRP's identifier and mode against its configuration, and now passes on only the members of the RRP's answer that the
CDDL gives its Freshness Kind and mode; it refuses (502) an answer with a Handle for an absent-* kind or without one for
present-nonce or present-epoch.

The requests. They no longer carry endorsements, which no draft defines; credential_type stays optional, as the
draft has it for Retrieval and this code had it in both (whether it travels is TheBankster/rats-tacra#19). A request
is refused with 400, saying why, unless it is what the CDDL defines: one JSON object in UTF-8 and nothing
after it; only the members the CDDL defines, each once, in its own case and of its own type, the required ones
present; a handle with every Freshness Kind but absent-none, and none with absent-none; each byte string unpadded
base64url as the control .b64u of RFC 9741 takes it (no padding, no line break, the bits that encode no octet zero).
Go's decoder alone takes a member name in any case, a member twice, null for a member, invalid UTF-8, and data after
the object: it took the first of two requests sent as one body. A body over the size limit is refused with 413. A
request refused for its Evidence format (415) no longer uses up its Handle: the server checks the format before it
correlates the Handle, in the order of the draft's processing (syntax and media type first).

Checked: go vet ./...; go test ./internal/tacra ./internal/refvectors ./cmd/estserver: ok, and no test binary links a
mock. TestAttestMediaTypes and TestAttestRequestSyntax serve the reference implementation's real requests (a GCP
SEV-SNP run) through the server's own router, with the CA label and without it: under eight media types, and as sent
and in 28 alterations, each refused for its reason; what is taken (the requests as sent, with white space after them,
an enrollment as absent-none without its handle, a retrieval without the optional credential_type) reaches the
backend, which serves no Target and refuses it with 403.
TestInitiationResponse makes the response of RRP answers as a run's gateways gave them, with members added that their
kind or mode does not take. TestRefEnvelopesRoundTrip: the reference implementation's messages decode with no member
unknown and encode back member for member, its attest-initiate responses once their rrp_id is taken out.
TestB64URLStrict: written as unpadded base64url, read only as .b64u takes it. TestUnreachable: an RRP that does not
answer gets 502, a verifier that does not answer 503, each a real TCP port nothing listens on.
TestFormatRefusalLeavesTheHandle: after a 415 for the Evidence format the Handle still serves its second leg. Each of
the eight checks this patch adds, turned off in turn, makes a test fail; so do the old order of the format and Handle
checks, and another status for an unreachable RRP or verifier.
